Chapter: Arm64Timer

 ARM64 Generic Timer driver. Uses the EL1 physical timer
 (CNTP) which fires PPI 30 (INTID 30) on the GIC.

 The timer frequency is read from CNTFRQ_EL0 at init time.
 Each tick reloads CNTP_TVAL_EL0 with freq/tick-rate,
 giving tick-rate ticks per second.

Section: Timer Constants

  timer-freq-addr : Integer = #80020
  timer-tick-rate : Integer = 100

Section: Timer Init

  arm64-timer-init : Integer -> Integer
  arm64-timer-init (dummy) =
   let freq = read-cntfrq-el0
   in let tval = freq / timer-tick-rate
   in let w1 = poke-qword timer-freq-addr 0 freq
   in let w2 = write-cntp-tval-el0 tval
   in let w3 = write-cntp-ctl-el0 1
   in 0

